{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/157416-dick-moves-aesir-edition","id":157416,"title":"Dick Moves: Aesir Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-02T21:06:42-07:00","id":157416,"title":"Dick Moves: Aesir Edition","content":"Here's io9's Dick Moves list when talking about the Aesir. There's some in there that I think was talked about in the previous thread, but also some more that seem new to me:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/10-of-the-norse-gods-biggest-dick-moves-1584842899\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/10-of-the-norse-gods-...ves-1584842899</a><br /> <br /> Kind of makes you wonder why they are the good guys again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T21:19:41-07:00","id":157432,"title":"","content":"I mean, from a Scion standpoint, it's because they don't want to reduce the world to roiling elemental chaos and leave mortals to their own business (for the most part) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2425-trueprep1818","name":"TruePrep1818","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T21:28:35-07:00","id":157456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/157416-dick-moves-aesir-edition#post157416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of makes you wonder why they are the good guys again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think this is one of the most interesting things about Scion. The Gods are, from a modern point of view, mostly monsters. The number of genuinely benelovent Gods I can count on my hands. I feel like it's a misconception that a lot of people have, but the cultures who developed these ideas rarely had the idea that their Gods were strictly 'good' people. Odin was womanly, The Morrigan is a monster, Aphrodite is kind of horrible to people, Zeus can't follow his own laws.<br /> <br /> Also, some of those bits are only 'bad' in a modern light. Always gotta remember that in the past, in the cultures that created these myths, a lot of this stuff was acceptable. #3 and #5 are normal things in that culture. All the bits where Dwarves are mistreated gotta be viewed through the lens that Dwarves are actually kind of horrible creatures who are personifications of greed, and have lust issues.<br /> <br /> Oh man, and Loki. Loki is actually probably the best member of the Aesir. He puts up with all of their cruelties towards him, solves all the problems (though he mainly starts them himself) and, even with Ragnarok, we've gotta remember that the whole story is super-duper fishy in the first place. It was written after the coming of the Christians, and Baldur looks incredibly suspiciously like Jesus. (Son, loved by all, light connections, comes back from the dead to lead the world into a bright new future after The Final Battle) So, Loki may have just caught the bad end of the stick when someone needed a bad guy.<br /> <br /> I think some interesting stuff can be done with the Ragnarok Prophecy if Loki isn't the Loki they are talking about. Utgard-Loki could do all of the things Loki is fated to do in that story, and we have already seen him as someone who has no love for the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Personally, my favorite bit of 'dickishness' from the Aesir, from a modern perspective, is how they have an entire Edda of the Norse Gods calling one and other gay. It's actually kind of hilarious in its absurdity. (Being gay, or 'womanly' was a Big Fucking Deal to the Norse)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T21:30:04-07:00","id":157457,"title":"","content":"I think very few gods are what we would consider 'Good Guys'. Most of them would be throwing around a bronze age mentality, and would be extremely racist and xenophobic. The best we can generally hope for is that protect the universe from being annihilated and leave us mostly alone. The periodic bouts of dickery are a small price to pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T17:24:11-07:00","id":158443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/157416-dick-moves-aesir-edition?p=157456#post157456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think this is one of the most interesting things about Scion. The Gods are, from a modern point of view, mostly monsters. The number of genuinely benelovent Gods I can count on my hands. I feel like it's a misconception that a lot of people have, but the cultures who developed these ideas rarely had the idea that their Gods were strictly 'good' people. Odin was womanly, The Morrigan is a monster, Aphrodite is kind of horrible to people, Zeus can't follow his own laws.<br /> <br /> Also, some of those bits are only 'bad' in a modern light. Always gotta remember that in the past, in the cultures that created these myths, a lot of this stuff was acceptable. #3 and #5 are normal things in that culture. All the bits where Dwarves are mistreated gotta be viewed through the lens that Dwarves are actually kind of horrible creatures who are personifications of greed, and have lust issues.<br /> <br /> Oh man, and Loki. Loki is actually probably the best member of the Aesir. He puts up with all of their cruelties towards him, solves all the problems (though he mainly starts them himself) and, even with Ragnarok, we've gotta remember that the whole story is super-duper fishy in the first place. It was written after the coming of the Christians, and Baldur looks incredibly suspiciously like Jesus. (Son, loved by all, light connections, comes back from the dead to lead the world into a bright new future after The Final Battle) So, Loki may have just caught the bad end of the stick when someone needed a bad guy.<br /> <br /> I think some interesting stuff can be done with the Ragnarok Prophecy if Loki isn't the Loki they are talking about. Utgard-Loki could do all of the things Loki is fated to do in that story, and we have already seen him as someone who has no love for the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Personally, my favorite bit of 'dickishness' from the Aesir, from a modern perspective, is how they have an entire Edda of the Norse Gods calling one and other gay. It's actually kind of hilarious in its absurdity. (Being gay, or 'womanly' was a Big Fucking Deal to the Norse)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get what you mean Watcher. When I looked read the inspirations for Mythical Detective Loki Ragnarok, in the Special Features section of the DVDs, they stated that there was an entirely different Edda out there that classified Loki, not as the God of Mischief as the Prose Edda claimed, but as Loki, Norse God of the Hearth, &quot;OF THE HEARTH&quot;. So if we follow this route, Loki was essentially the Aesir version of Hestia of the Olympians, and he watched over Asgard's inner sanctum while Heimdall watched the borders. I wondered to myself, &quot;Why didn't we hear about this?&quot;. Not only the hair-cutting episode of the myths was there, but also there was a thing where Loki apparently took out one of Heimdall's eyes, and Heimdall was butt-sore about it from then on.<br /> <br /> As for the show, Loki actually met Utgard-Loki in the series, which made me think that there were two Lokis : Utgard-Loki, who probably cemented the God of Mischief moniker in common memory, due to the fact that he shared Loki's name somewhat, and Loki himself, who was a hearth god.<br /> <br /> If you want to know more about this different Loki, I would recommend watching the anime (and the following manga if you can find it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:25:18-07:00","id":158507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/157416-dick-moves-aesir-edition?p=158443#post158443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I get what you mean Watcher. When I looked read the inspirations for Mythical Detective Loki Ragnarok, in the Special Features section of the DVDs, they stated that there was an entirely different Edda out there that classified Loki, not as the God of Mischief as the Prose Edda claimed, but as Loki, Norse God of the Hearth, &quot;OF THE HEARTH&quot;. So if we follow this route, Loki was essentially the Aesir version of Hestia of the Olympians, and he watched over Asgard's inner sanctum while Heimdall watched the borders. I wondered to myself, &quot;Why didn't we hear about this?&quot;. Not only the hair-cutting episode of the myths was there, but also there was a thing where Loki apparently took out one of Heimdall's eyes, and Heimdall was butt-sore about it from then on.<br /> <br /> As for the show, Loki actually met Utgard-Loki in the series, which made me think that there were two Lokis : Utgard-Loki, who probably cemented the God of Mischief moniker in common memory, due to the fact that he shared Loki's name somewhat, and Loki himself, who was a hearth god.<br /> <br /> If you want to know more about this different Loki, I would recommend watching the anime (and the following manga if you can find it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I... Do you know which Edda that's from and where that eye myth is from? I have never, ever heard of either of those. I know there is a general misconception as Loki being a Fire God which is based on a Linguistic connection someone made about two hundred years ago connecting Loki with Logi, the word for fire, which I'm fairly sure was thrown out as either being a bad translation, or so tangential and without other evidence, it is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Loki was defiantly the God of Mischief, like, without a doubt. That is something that is undoubtedly true, and we have mountains of evidence for. You are entirely welcome to use this Anime's representation of Loki for Loki in your games though. We just are very, very focused on original sources and so on to get things just right, or as right as we can manage.<br /> <br /> But, if you remember which Edda this is, or if you have the spare time to check out the commentary again and point me in the right direction, I would love to go back and reread them to see this mention of Loki being a Hearth God and that myth about him maiming Heimdall. I know he and Heimdall wrestled to a standstill, Loki being a Giant and all, he is incredibly strong and so on, but I never heard about him taking one of Heimdall's eyes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Memb